{
  "note": "Tokens declared somewhere the scope that needs them cannot reach. FREEZE: a `:root` declaration that reads a re-scopable seed substitutes once on <html>, so a scope below it inherits the answer root gave — the cure is `--x: initial` with the formula at the call site (docs/TOKENS.md). REACH: a bare `var(--t)` on an element where --t computes to nothing, because --t is declared only under a selector that element is not inside. Every entry is DEBT and the list may only SHRINK; the gate fails on anything new. Keyed on the ARRANGEMENT and never on a frame, an element or a measured value — a pixel in the key makes every known entry read as new on a different renderer (preview/frame-overflow.baseline.json learned that the hard way). `seenOn` is where to go and look.",
  "tracked": "gh#834 + gh#835 opened this list. Both are FIXED here and neither is in it: the --font-size-* ramp is `initial` at the tier with its formula at the call site (19 FREEZE entries retired), and --space-inline-xl is declared at :root beside the other four steps (1 REACH entry retired).\n  WHAT IS LEFT, AND WHAT IT IS. Every remaining FREEZE entry is a `:root` declaration that reads a seed docs/CUSTOMER-THEMING.md tells a consumer they may re-scope, so a [data-tenant] or .dark subtree that sets that seed will NOT move the knob. The colour half is the gh#687 / control-surface shape and is the dangerous half (a frozen light surface under dark ink). The --radius-* and --shadow-* families are the same defect as the type ramp, one tier over, and are the obvious next tranche: six steps each, the same `initial` + call-site-formula repair.\n  NOT IN THIS LIST, ON PURPOSE: the ~230 component tokens that mirror a foundation step at :root (`--badge-font-size: var(--font-size-xs)`). They are frozen too, and they are the third tranche; see the tier clause in scripts/check-frame-token-scope.mjs for the measurement that kept them out of the gate rather than out of the truth.",
